    "user_request_original": "Optimize an 18-layer TiO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica substrate at 45° incidence. Initialize layer thicknesses as follows in nm: [174.64, 197.98, 183.72, 98.09, 166.23, 298.71, 56.66, 85.03, 215.43, 90.06, 173.07, 225.90, 168.16, 115.01, 205.04, 100.50, 200.69, 107.02]. Apply harmonic perturbation to layers 6-9: thickness_6 = 298.71 * (1 + 0.15*sin(pi*6/10)), thickness_7 = 56.66 * (1 + 0.15*sin(pi*7/10)), thickness_8 = 85.03 * (1 + 0.15*sin(pi*8/10)), thickness_9 = 215.43 * (1 + 0.15*sin(pi*9/10)). Allow all 18 thicknesses to optimize within 50-300nm bounds using gradient-based optimizer. Evaluate reflectance in 450-650nm band and transmittance in 700-1000nm band at 45° incidence for unpolarized light. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 450-650 nm, 700-1000 nm. soft objectives: high reflectance in 450-650 nm; high transmittance in 700-1000 nm; minimized crosstalk between bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 450-650 nm; reflectance in 700-1000 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 24 layers.",
